    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Boys with an occupation in Manlleu, 1905"
    description: |-
      A study of children's work in the Catalan textile town of Manlleu, reporting the share of boys with a recorded occupation in 1905 on two age bases: ages 8-14 and ages 10-14.

      Manlleu is a textile town rather than a national sample, and rates of this size were matched only in the Catalan textile districts.
    date_published: "2011"

